WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:05.645
Enceladus is the sixth-largest moon of Saturn and the 18th largest in the Solar System.

00:06.161 --> 00:12.471
It is about 500 kilometres in diameter, about a tenth of that of Saturn's largest moon, Titan.

00:13.021 --> 00:21.224
It is covered by clean, freshly deposited snow hundreds of meters thick, making it one of the most reflective bodies of the Solar System.

00:21.717 --> 00:30.922
Consequently, its surface temperature at noon reaches only −198 °C, far colder than a light-absorbing body would be.

00:31.572 --> 00:42.406
Despite its small size, Enceladus has a wide variety of surface features, ranging from old, heavily cratered regions to young, tectonically deformed terrain.
